# 7️⃣ Balanced Binary Tree

## 📖 Problem

Determine whether a Binary Tree is height-balanced.

A tree is balanced if the height difference between the left and right subtrees of every node is at most:

```text
1
```

That is:

```text
|Left Height - Right Height| <= 1
```

---

### Example

Balanced:

```text
        1
       / \
      2   3
     / \
    4   5
```

---

### Unbalanced:

```text
        1
       /
      2
     /
    3
   /
  4
```

---

## 💡 Efficient Approach

Calculate height while checking balance.

If an unbalanced subtree is found, return:

```text
-1
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
int checkHeight(Node* root)
{
    if(root == NULL)
        return 0;

    int leftHeight = checkHeight(root->left);

    if(leftHeight == -1)
        return -1;

    int rightHeight = checkHeight(root->right);

    if(rightHeight == -1)
        return -1;

    if(abs(leftHeight - rightHeight) > 1)
        return -1;

    return 1 + max(leftHeight, rightHeight);
}

bool isBalanced(Node* root)
{
    return checkHeight(root) != -1;
}
```

---

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(n)

Space: O(h)
```

